meta:
  origin:
    producer: World Health Organization
    title: "WHO Growth Reference: Height-for-age, 5-19 years"
    description: |-
      The WHO Growth Reference for school-aged children and adolescents extends the WHO Child Growth Standards beyond age 5. It was constructed by merging the 1977 NCHS/WHO growth reference sample with the cross-sectional sample underlying the under-fives standards, then smoothing the result so that the curves transition smoothly into the under-fives standards at age 5.

      The height-for-age reference covers months 61 to 228, tabulated by month of age.

      These are the expanded tables, which WHO publishes so that countries can reproduce the growth charts on national health cards. They give the L, M, and S parameters of the fitted distribution alongside percentiles and z-scores at three-decimal precision. For height-for-age they also include a -5 SD cut-off, used to assess very short stature.
    citation_full: |-
      de Onis M, Onyango AW, Borghi E, Siyam A, Nishida C, Siekmann J. Development of a WHO growth reference for school-aged children and adolescents. Bulletin of the World Health Organization. 2007;85(9):660-667.
    attribution_short: WHO
    url_main: https://www.who.int/tools/growth-reference-data-for-5to19-years/indicators/height-for-age
